{% doc %}
  The skip link.

  First focusable element in the document, hidden until focused. Every keyboard
  and screen reader user meets it before anything else, which is the point: on a
  store with a mega menu, the alternative is thirty tab presses to reach the
  product they came for.

  It is a real anchor to `#MainContent`, and `global.js` moves focus to the
  target after the jump — without that, browsers scroll but leave focus at the
  top, so the next Tab goes back into the header.

  Parameters:
    target (string, optional)  Defaults to MainContent

  @example
    {% render 'skip-to-content' %}
{% enddoc %}

<a
  class="skip-to-content-link button visually-hidden"
  href="#{{ target | default: 'MainContent' }}"
>
  {{ 'accessibility.skip_to_content' | t }}
</a>
